#🦉



I'm happy to share that we decided to open source a AI coding tool we've developed internally at Covenance.ai - kodo 🦉

, coding agent orchestrator. It is MIT licensed.



https://github.com/ikamensh/kodo



Why kodo? Coding agents became real good, real fast. But they are not really independent — they only do work step at a time, forcing you to sit in front of the terminal / UI waiting. Don’t get me wrong, usually you make a difference by guiding AI. But sometimes you just want to let it do the best it can leveraging more time and compute, not your attention.



You need to have an AI coding tool to use kodo, it does not replace claude code / cursor, it orchestrates their work toward a goal you set. It has two modes - building towards a high-level goal (put it in goal.md or type in terminal) and --improve mode - just test your project thoroughly, improve architecture and test coverage, where it needs no further input from you at all.



Its also possible to run Kodo in free tier using google-cli that google generously allows for free users just with google account.



I hope projects README to be enough to get you started. Happy to hear your feedback! its a work in progress, but in the fast paced world of AI I decided to share it since we already see significant value from it as it is now. Enjoy! ;) And you are explicitly welcome to propose features and report any problems, usability or bugs at https://github.com/ikamensh/kodo





Fun fact: 99% of kodo is written by claude code and kodo itself




